## compose_flip.rs SERVICE_PENDING
Nothing: this task registers no protocol method and no service. The module is a library the Office tool's service (a later task of
the office track) calls: `tabular::{create, snapshot, apply_batch, validate, issues}` take a `ReadProof`/`WriteProof` of
mixdog-fsio, a `&dyn mixdog_office_base::write_note::WriteNote` (the call's ledger: noted before every write) and JSON operations and
options, and answer JSON values with Node's exact key order and texts; `Format::from_name("csv" | "tsv")` picks the format and
`tabular::csv_cell` is `csvCell` of office-actions-read.mjs for the PDF table export.


## Corrective implementation (pending fresh Node recording and compiled review)

The guessed 120,000-item spread cap is removed. Array.from's ToLength/ordinary
Array length bound remains. insert_empty reserves the full Vec capacity with
try_reserve, appends default empty entries, then rotates the existing suffix;
there is no argument spread, intermediate insertion array or quadratic sequence
of middle inserts. A failed reservation returns Invalid array length before that
vector changes; an error anywhere in a batch leaves the file and WriteNote untouched.

The original V8 argument-stack failure is contextual, not a portable data bound.
Bounded original-expression probes accepted 120001 and 122000 arguments and threw
Maximum call stack size exceeded at 125000 on this Node run. No replacement guessed
cap is introduced. Above the tested old-supported range, this stackless backend
can accept operations the original spread would fail; exact engine-stack resource
failure parity is NOT claimed. Heap/resource exhaustion is likewise not a stable
cross-runtime semantic threshold. Do not label those extended counts Node-verified.

snapshot/issues now distinguish explicit Value::Null (the original TypeErrors on
'sheet'/'range') from omitted options. Callers MUST represent omitted options with
an empty JSON object, not Null. Reads still happen before option-property access,
so an absent file wins with ENOENT. Twin run_step makes this distinction.

New deterministic regression tests:
- inserts_above_the_old_guessed_cap_keep_every_existing_cell (120001/122000 rows and columns)
- explicit_null_options_fail_after_reading_and_omitted_options_are_an_object
- bom_only_and_failed_batch_preserve_bytes_and_write_note_order
The note captures actual pre-write bytes; failed batches make no note call.

The Node recorder now includes bounded insertion, omitted/null, missing-file,
BOM-only and failed-batch scenarios. Long file outputs now carry SHA-256 plus
length. The existing four length-only wide-row read steps are replayed against
their complete initial bytes, so old fixtures do not retain a length-only escape.

IMPORTANT: the worktree already had a deleted tracked
benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/lib/common.mjs before this corrective task. That
unrelated deletion is preserved and was not restored/staged/reset. Therefore the
updated recorder was NOT executed and existing golden.json/MANIFEST.json are
unchanged; no new oracle outputs have been fabricated. Root must run the updated
recorder from its full integration tree and refresh the set/root manifest hashes
and totalBytes. The old index size above describes the old recorded set only.

No Cargo/build/Rust test/app/commit was run. After registration, dependencies and
fresh recording, run the unit regressions and twin_tabular offline, then clippy.

## Root integration status

Library export and dependency edges applied in mig/int. Fresh original recording
contains 84 scenarios, replayed exactly together with unit regressions (28 tests).
Large file outputs compare SHA-256 and byte length. No product office.run routing
activation or Node removal was performed by this integration.
